# Scheduler observability (Prompt 01 section 7). Committed because the QUESTION is historical:
# "is the observed cadence degrading" cannot be answered by a file that only ever holds the
# current run. Both are small — one JSON object each, no per-row data.
!output/scheduler_health.json
!output/high_activity_coverage.json
# Per-table import accounting for the builder evidence: rows seen, imported, skipped as
# duplicates, canonical total. Committed because "the importer ran" and "the importer stored
# anything" are different claims, and only the second one is worth alarming on.
!output/combo_import_health.json
!output/output_manifest.json

# The season store IS the deliverable and must survive across CI runs, so it is committed.
# Safe to commit because writes are run-partitioned (one small file per table per run) and
# the append-only histories are watermarked — a repeat run adds nothing.
!data/season_*/
!data/season_*/**
# Watermarks must persist or every run re-imports v9's full odds history (~40k rows).
!output/import_watermarks.json

# The git-history extract (935 fixtures). Committed so the results fetch can run in CI WITHOUT
# cloning v9's 1.3GB history: the extract needs all 702 predictions.csv commits, the results
# fetch needs none of them. Also means the expensive walk is done once, not per run.
!data/_backfill_fixtures.parquet

# The JOINED result — and the gate for pro_backfill_results.yml, which skips when this exists.
# MUST be committed or the gate can never see it and the hourly schedule would redo the whole
# fetch forever. Caught before shipping: `data/**` above would otherwise have ignored it.
!data/_backfill_joined.parquet
# The resolver version that produced the join above. MUST be committed alongside it: the workflow
# gate compares this to RESOLVER_VERSION in the source to decide whether an improvement to
# club-name resolution needs re-applying. Ignored, it would read as version 0 forever and the job
# would redo the whole fetch on every schedule.
!data/_backfill_resolver_version
!registry/**
!experiments/**/manifest.json
!experiments/**/metrics.json
!experiments/**/by_league.csv
!experiments/**/calibration.csv

